 "edits": [
  {
   "op": "replace_brief",
   "brief": "pc-typical",
   "html": "<div class=\"brief sp pc\" id=\"pc-typical\" data-entry=\"card\" data-lens=\"psych\" data-spine=\"2\" data-shelf=\"psych\" data-bp=\"behav\" data-navgrp=\"02 Antipsychotics\" data-sys=\"psych-pharm\">\n<p class=\"pc-grp\">02 Antipsychotics <span>&middot;</span> class card</p>\n<h4>Typical antipsychotics</h4>\n<p class=\"sub\">first-generation antipsychotics &middot; chlorpromazine &middot; fluphenazine &middot; haloperidol &middot; loxapine &middot; molindone &middot; perphenazine &middot; pimozide &middot; thioridazine &middot; thiothixene &middot; trifluoperazine</p>\n<div class=\"dp\"><span class=\"lbl\">Key point</span><ul class=\"bl\">\n<li><b>Typical antipsychotics</b> block <b>dopamine D2</b> receptors <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> fewer positive symptoms; little effect on negative symptoms</li>\n<li><b>High potency</b> (haloperidol, fluphenazine): more <b>extrapyramidal effects</b>; <b>low potency</b> (chlorpromazine, thioridazine): more <b>sedation</b>, dry mouth, <b>orthostasis</b></li>\n<li>More <b>neuroleptic malignant syndrome (NMS)</b> and <b>tardive dyskinesia</b> than atypical drugs; <b>QT</b>: low potency, IV haloperidol and pimozide</li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"sp-script sp-s2 pc-script\"><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Drugs</span><div class=\"sv\"><p><b>Chlorpromazine</b>: low potency; corneal deposits; purple-gray skin in sun, jaundice <span class=\"sp-k\">Mnemonic</span><span class=\"sp-vl\" data-src=\"AnKing\"><span class=\"sp-ct\">Eye deposits</span>\"<b>C</b>hlorpromazine for <b>C</b>orneal, Thio<b>R</b>idazine for <b>R</b>etinal.\"</span></p><p><b><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop sp-a\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pctyp-pop-2\">Fluphenazine</button></b>: high potency; decanoate depot <span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pctyp-pop-2\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Thermoregulation</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Phenothiazines such as fluphenazine: impair temperature control</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Poor tolerance of heat and of cold</span></span></p><p><b>Haloperidol</b>: high potency, most extrapyramidal effects; decanoate depot; QT when IV</p><p><b>Loxapine</b> <span class=\"pc-tn\">Adasuve</span>: an inhaled powder form</p><p><b>Molindone</b>: may cause weight loss</p><p><b>Perphenazine</b>: mid potency</p><p><b>Pimozide</b>: high potency; Tourette tics; QT, many barred pairs</p><p><b>Thioridazine</b>: low potency; <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop sp-a\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pctyp-pop-3\">retinal deposits</button>; QT <span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pctyp-pop-3\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Thioridazine retinopathy</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Pigment change can mimic retinitis pigmentosa</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Daily dose ceiling of 800 mg exists to prevent retinopathy</span></span></p><p><b>Thiothixene</b>: high rate of akathisia</p><p><b>Trifluoperazine</b>: high potency</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Mechanism</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>Mesolimbic <b>D2 block</b> <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> fewer hallucinations and delusions</p><p>Nigrostriatal D2 block<button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop sp-i\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pctyp-pop-4\" aria-label=\"More information\"></button> <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> acetylcholine outweighs dopamine <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> <b>extrapyramidal effects</b> <span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pctyp-pop-4\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">D2-blocking antiemetics</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Metoclopramide and prochlorperazine: block D2 as well</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Can cause the same movement effects</span></span></p><p>Tuberoinfundibular D2 block <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> <b>prolactin</b> rises</p><p>Low potency: <b>muscarinic</b>, <b>histamine</b> and <b>alpha-1</b> block <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> dry mouth, sedation, orthostasis</p><p>Years of D2 block <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> receptor <b>upregulation</b>, supersensitivity <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> tardive dyskinesia</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Uses</span><div class=\"sv\"><p><b>Psychosis</b>: positive symptoms; atypical drugs usually preferred <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"psychosis-duration\">Psychosis</button></p><p><b>Agitation</b>: acute mania; refractory delirium (haloperidol) <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"bipolar-mania\">Bipolar Disorder</button> <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"delirium\">Delirium</button></p><p><b>Tourette</b> tics that resist standard treatment: haloperidol, fluphenazine, pimozide <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"tics\">Tics and Tic Disorders</button></p><p><b>Depot</b> for missed doses: haloperidol, fluphenazine <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"sz-psychosocial\">Schizophrenia: Long-Term Care</button></p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Adverse effects</span><div class=\"sv\"><p><b><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop sp-a\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pctyp-pop-5\">Movement</button></b>: dystonia, akathisia, parkinsonism, tardive dyskinesia; most with high potency <span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pctyp-pop-5\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Risk factors for movement effects</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Dystonia: likeliest in young men</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Parkinsonism, tardive dyskinesia: likeliest in older women</span></span> <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"antipsych-effects\">Antipsychotic Adverse Effects</button></p><p><b>Prolactin</b>: amenorrhea, galactorrhea, gynecomastia, sexual dysfunction <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"prolactin\">Hyperprolactinemia</button></p><p><b>QT</b>, torsades: thioridazine, chlorpromazine, IV haloperidol, pimozide</p><p><b>Anticholinergic</b>, sedation, orthostasis: low potency</p><p><b>Weight</b>, glucose, lipids: less than atypical drugs; most with low potency</p><p><b>Seizure threshold</b> lowered</p><p><b>Dementia</b>: higher death rate in older adults, somewhat more than with atypical drugs <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"antipsych-effects\">Antipsychotic Adverse Effects</button></p></div></div></div>\n<div class=\"sp-rows pc-blocks\">\n<div class=\"sp-row\"><span class=\"sp-src\">Neuroleptic malignant syndrome</span><b class=\"sp-f\">Fever, lead-pipe rigidity, confusion, unstable vital signs; more often than with atypical drugs</b><div class=\"sp-chips\"> <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"antipsych-effects\">Antipsychotic Adverse Effects</button></div><p class=\"sp-commit\"><b>If</b> it is suspected, <b>choose</b> <span class=\"mask\">stopping the antipsychotic, then cooling and IV fluids</span>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"sp-row\"><span class=\"sp-src\">QT prolongation</span><b class=\"sp-f\">Thioridazine, chlorpromazine, IV haloperidol, pimozide; torsades and sudden death</b><p class=\"sp-commit\"><b>If</b> pimozide is started, <b>choose</b> <span class=\"mask\">an electrocardiogram at baseline and through dose changes</span>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"sp-row\"><span class=\"sp-src\">Acute dystonia</span><b class=\"sp-f\">Neck, jaw, tongue or eye spasm; laryngeal spasm can block the airway</b><div class=\"sp-chips\"> <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"antipsych-effects\">Antipsychotic Adverse Effects</button></div><p class=\"sp-commit\"><b>If</b> a young man or a past reactor gets intramuscular haloperidol, <b>choose</b> <span class=\"mask\">benztropine or diphenhydramine with the dose</span>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"sp-row\"><span class=\"sp-src\">Dementia with Lewy bodies (Lewy body dementia)</span><b class=\"sp-f\">Severe parkinsonism and clouded consciousness after a dose</b><div class=\"sp-chips\"> <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"parkinson\">Parkinson Disease and Parkinsonism</button></div><p class=\"sp-commit\"><b>If</b> it is present, <b>choose</b> <span class=\"mask\">avoiding typical antipsychotics</span>.</p></div>\n</div>\n<figure class=\"lcw pc-lcw\"><div class=\"ttl\"><span>Onset of extrapyramidal effects and neuroleptic malignant syndrome</span><small>not to scale</small></div><div class=\"wax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">0</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:18%\">hours</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:36%\">days</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:54%\">weeks</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:72%\">months</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:90%\">years</span><em>&rarr;</em></div></div><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Acute dystonia</b><span class=\"win\">Hours to days; usually by 48 hours</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:18%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:36%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:54%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:72%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:90%\"></i><i class=\"bar c3\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:36%\"></i></div><p class=\"wl\">painful twisting of neck, jaw or eyes</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Akathisia</b><span class=\"win\">Usually hours to days; up to months</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:18%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:36%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:54%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:72%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:90%\"></i><i class=\"bar c2\" style=\"--a:9%;--b:72%\"></i></div><p class=\"wl\">inner restlessness, often pacing; most common extrapyramidal effect</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Drug-induced parkinsonism</b><span class=\"win\">Days to weeks</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:18%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:36%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:54%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:72%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:90%\"></i><i class=\"bar c2\" style=\"--a:27%;--b:63%\"></i></div><p class=\"wl\">tremor on both sides, rigidity, slowness</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Neuroleptic malignant syndrome</b><span class=\"win\">Usually the first 2 weeks; possible any time</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:18%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:36%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:54%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:72%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:90%\"></i><i class=\"bar c3\" style=\"--a:27%;--b:60%\"></i></div><p class=\"wl\">fever, rigidity; can build over 1 to 3 days</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop sp-a\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pctyp-pop-6\">Tardive dyskinesia</button></b><span class=\"win\">Usually after more than 6 months <span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pctyp-pop-6\" data-src=\"MSD Manual\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Cumulative risk</span><span class=\"sp-l\">With typical drugs the risk adds up</span><span class=\"sp-l\">About 5% per year of use</span></span></span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:18%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:36%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:54%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:72%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:90%\"></i><i class=\"bar c2\" style=\"--a:66%;--b:90%\"></i></div><p class=\"wl\">lip smacking, tongue thrusting; often unnoticed by the patient</p></div></li></ol></figure>\n<div class=\"sp-dx pc-tbl\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Drug interactions</caption><thead><tr><th>Drug</th><th>Effect</th><th>Management</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Another QT drug: macrolide, fluoroquinolone, tricyclic</td><td><span>Added QT prolongation, torsades</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Caution; electrocardiogram if at risk</span></span></td></tr><tr><td><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop sp-a\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pctyp-pop-7\">Pimozide plus clarithromycin</button>, itraconazole or ketoconazole <span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pctyp-pop-7\" data-src=\"pimozide label\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Pimozide pairs</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Also barred with pimozide: sertraline, citalopram, escitalopram</span><span class=\"sp-l\">Also barred with pimozide: any other QT-prolonging drug</span></span></td><td><span>Sudden deaths reported with clarithromycin</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Contraindicated</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"sp-dx pc-tbl\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Monitoring</caption><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>Check</th><th>Rationale</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>From the start</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Weight, glucose, lipids, blood pressure</span></span></td><td><span>Metabolic harm <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"antipsych-effects\">Antipsychotic Adverse Effects</button></span></td></tr><tr><td>About every 6 months</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Abnormal movements</span></span></td><td><span>Tardive dyskinesia</span></td></tr><tr><td>Every year</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Prolactin symptoms; a level if present</span></span></td><td><span>Hyperprolactinemia</span></td></tr><tr><td>Heart disease or several drugs</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Electrocardiogram</span></span></td><td><span>QT prolongation</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"pc-owners\"><span class=\"lbl\">Drug choice by condition</span>\n<p>Which drug for schizophrenia <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"psychosis-duration\">Psychosis</button></p>\n<p>Long-acting injections for missed doses <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"sz-psychosocial\">Schizophrenia: Long-Term Care</button></p>\n<p>Naming and treating each movement effect and neuroleptic malignant syndrome <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"antipsych-effects\">Antipsychotic Adverse Effects</button></p>\n<p>What the anticholinergic drugs relieve <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"pc-antichol\">Anticholinergic</button></p>\n<p>Drugs for tardive dyskinesia <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"pc-td\">Tardive dyskinesia agents</button></p>\n<p>Haloperidol for delirium agitation <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"delirium\">Delirium</button></p>\n<p>Which drug for Tourette tics <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"tics\">Tics and Tic Disorders</button></p>\n</div>\n\n<h5 class=\"authored-hdr\" id=\"pctyp-bank\">Practice</h5>\n<ol class=\"bank authored\">\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Chlorpromazine\" data-d2=\"Haloperidol\" data-item-id=\"q_40c6bf324384e5c7712b\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_76f3c8b74b16aac5a40b\" data-d1-id=\"o_b2075cdd5b3feee09c55\" data-d2-id=\"o_38f843690a1c258b78dc\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which antipsychotic is he most likely taking?\" data-key-why=\"Low potency, with pigment deposits in the retina and QT prolongation\" data-d1-why=\"Low potency too, but its deposits are in the cornea, with sun-exposed skin changes\" data-d2-why=\"High potency: extrapyramidal effects, little sedation or dry mouth\"><span class=\"sl\">52-year-old man with schizophrenia on the same low-potency antipsychotic for years</span>\n<span class=\"si\">gradually dimming vision in both eyes</span>\n<span class=\"si\">dry mouth and daytime drowsiness; corrected QT 490 ms</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">fundus exam: pigment deposits across both retinas</span> &rarr; <b>Thioridazine</b> &rarr; retinal deposits that can mimic retinitis pigmentosa, plus QT prolongation</li>\n<li data-type=\"mech\" data-d1=\"Nigrostriatal D2 blockade\" data-d2=\"Tuberoinfundibular D2 blockade\" data-item-id=\"q_2fa7ae1401fda27a738f\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_4148ac5780c0123954f4\" data-d1-id=\"o_771a43abf9575a2a6093\" data-d2-id=\"o_40fcdd47fe0bd72a01eb\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which receptor action best explains these effects?\" data-key-why=\"Low potency: off-target block gives orthostasis, dry mouth, constipation and sedation\" data-d1-why=\"Gives stiffness, tremor or restlessness; none is present\" data-d2-why=\"Raises prolactin: missed periods, breast discharge; not these signs\"><span class=\"sl\">40-year-old woman with schizophrenia started chlorpromazine 1 week ago</span>\n<span class=\"si\">lightheaded on standing; pulse rises from 78 to 104/min</span>\n<span class=\"si\">dry mouth, constipation, sleepy through the day</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">no stiffness, tremor or restlessness</span> &rarr; <b>Alpha-1, muscarinic and histamine blockade</b> &rarr; the low-potency profile: less D2 binding, more off-target block</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Amoxicillin\" data-d2=\"Doxycycline\" data-item-id=\"q_d6b90a2a436c98b15996\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_10940d2dffe758daac9e\" data-d1-id=\"o_ac42a7b67f31598eb5db\" data-d2-id=\"o_88d40a807b5a2487fb76\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which newly added drug most likely caused this?\" data-key-why=\"A macrolide: it prolongs QT itself, and the pimozide label bars it; sudden deaths were reported with clarithromycin\" data-d1-why=\"A penicillin; not among the QT-prolonging antibiotics\" data-d2-why=\"A tetracycline; not among the QT-prolonging antibiotics\"><span class=\"sl\">16-year-old boy with Tourette syndrome takes pimozide after haloperidol failed</span>\n<span class=\"si\">started a new drug 3 days ago for community-acquired pneumonia</span>\n<span class=\"si\">fainted at school after palpitations</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">electrocardiogram: corrected QT 560 ms, polymorphic ventricular runs</span> &rarr; <b>Clarithromycin</b> &rarr; pimozide is contraindicated with macrolides and other QT-prolonging drugs</li>\n</ol>\n</div>",
